  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 132 AM CDT Sun May 31 2026\n\nWe will see one more dry day before rain chances return beginning \nMonday. Expect warmer conditions through this week with highs in the \n80s and 90s across the region with heat indices around 100-105. This \nwill lead to minor to moderate heat stress conditions. \n\nThe chances for showers and storms will return to the region this \nweek as the ridge weakens allowing for some shortwave energy to \ncreep into the region which will combine with the seabreeze each \nday. This will be coupled with a surge of moisture thanks to the \nreturn of onshore flow this evening. A low to medium chance for \nshowers and thunderstorms will exist through this upcoming weekend \nbeginning with low chances Monday. Chances will increase to around a \nmedium chance. The highest chances for rainfall will be during each \nafternoon. Activity will continue until the evening with the loss of \ndaytime heating.",
